Forwarding Cognition's latest public announcement, summarized for diligence.

Cognition has raised over $2B at a $48B valuation in its Series E (September 8, 2026).
The round was led by new investors Andreessen Horowitz and Accel, alongside existing investors Founders Fund, General Catalyst, and Avenir. Other investors include Benchmark, Bessemer, Kleiner Perkins, Greylock, Lightspeed, Altimeter, Bond Capital, Meritech, T. Rowe Price, Lux, and 8VC.
Since its last round in May, Cognition's run-rate revenue has grown from $492M to almost $900M.
The previous round, in May 2026, raised over $1B at a $26B valuation, led by Lux Capital, General Catalyst, and 8VC.
Devin powers engineering teams at NVIDIA, GE Aerospace, Citi, Mercedes-Benz, and Modal.
Cognition has hubs in San Francisco, New York, and Austin, and opened offices in Washington, D.C., Tokyo, Singapore, London, Sao Paulo, and Madrid in the past year.

